1
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:13,360
Brighten up the peace, then step away, okay?

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
Those who leave right
after the night is over.

4
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:35,520
Wa-wa-ra, uwa-wa-wa-ra.

5
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:40,020
Wappara-pu-wachi-wappara.

6
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:45,560
Don't rush, in this narrow town.

7
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,400
Where are you going?
Haste makes waste, so take the long way.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,680
Maybe, more than me,

9
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,520
if there's someone better,

10
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:02,980
tell me, tell me all night long.

11
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,680
Wappara-pu-wachiwa.

12
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:17,020
I don't mind waiting,
because I'm a Kameza woman.

13
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,680
I won't lose, I'm a Ginza woman.

14
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:29,860
I'll love you for years,
the everyday life of a Kameza woman.

15
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,760
Ryotsu Stamina Co., Ltd.

16
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,240
W-what? Marriage?

17
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:48,140
K-Kan-chan, don't shout so loud!

18
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,460
How could I not shout at this?

19
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:54,500
Why is Konta getting
married when I'm still single?

20
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,060
W-well,
you can't expect me to just accept that...

21
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:59,580
Shiori, was it?

22
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:00,540
Yes.

23
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,840
And you're still in your twenties.

24
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:07,740
Why would you decide to marry Konta,
the defector from Tonchinkankon?

25
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,720
Tonchinkankon?

26
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:14,780
Tonpei and Chinkichi,
who were close friends since childhood...

27
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:19,900
Kan-chan, you, and I were a group of four, and we were called Tonchinkankon,
taking the first letter from each of our names.

28
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:30,380
Tonpei de ton! Chinkichi de chin!
Kankichi de kaan!

29
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,320
What are you doing, Konta?

30
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,000
Konta-deko

31
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,360
All four of us together: kon-chin-kan!

32
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:41,620
Kon

33
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:47,720
Konta, your timing is terrible!

34
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,460
If we don't keep the
tonchinkankon rhythm snappy...

35
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:53,860
But it's embarrassing, Kan-chan.

36
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:58,260
Even though Konta is the
low-key one in Tonchinkankon,

37
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,900
but if we take a photo...

38
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,080
Let's go! Let's go!

39
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,720
Yeah!

40
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,160
Even when we go on a field trip...

41
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:14,540
Is everyone here? Is anyone missing?

42
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,360
No one is missing!

43
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:17,820
Well then, please go ahead.

44
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:19,160
Sure.

45
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,900
I feel like we're forgetting something.

46
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,660
Now that you mention it, I do feel that way.

47
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:27,060
But try to remember...

48
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:28,860
Why-!

49
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,600
Oh no! Konta!

50
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:34,500
Wait up!

51
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,880
You can't just leave me behind!

52
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:41,420
Teacher! We forgot Konta! Stop the bus!

53
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,100
What?!

54
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,966
And that's how it went,

55
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:48,800
and in the end, Tonchinkankon somehow
turned into just Tonchinkan, didn't it?

56
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:52,413
Heh, actually, the reason we started dating

57
00:03:52,463 --> 00:03:55,960
was a bus tour planned by a travel company.

58
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:08,720
Guide, the person in the
seat ahead isn't on the bus.

59
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:14,780
Hey, leaving me behind is cruel!

60
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,560
If you hadn't noticed,
I would have been left behind.

61
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:24,300
Thank you so much.

62
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:28,360
Thanks. Would you like one?

63
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:34,920
Then I'll take one.
That's how we started dating.

64
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:41,720
After that, similar things happened a few times,
and I felt I had to stay by Konta's side.

65
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:47,160
So your maternal instincts were stirred?
Yeah, well...

66
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:52,660
Konta, you lucky dog. She's beautiful and has a sweet temper,
this girl.

67
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,400
Anyway, this is just wonderful!

68
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,420
Alright, I'll be the MC for
the wedding reception myself.

69
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:00,960
So, when's the wedding?

70
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,280
What's going on?

71
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:09,340
Kan-chan, we've decided not
to have a wedding ceremony.

72
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:11,080
Why not?

73
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:15,040
The company I work for has been running in the red,
you see.

74
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:18,040
No bonus, and a 20% pay cut.

75
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,500
We can't really afford a ceremony.

76
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,220
It's the recession, after all.

77
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:25,020
But is that really alright, Shiori?

78
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:31,780
I'm happy just to be with Konta-san,
even without a ceremony.

79
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,800
Uuugh, you're making me cry!

80
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,920
Really, you found yourself a good bride.

81
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:40,240
Alright, I'll make sure you
have your wedding ceremony.

82
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,840
K-Kan-chan?

83
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,700
Don't worry about the money.

84
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:44,700
B-but...

85
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:47,920
It's fine. Leave it all to me!

86
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,400
Is that really Konta?

87
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,580
Lend us the wedding hall you run, will you?

88
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,340
I understand the situation well enough.

89
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:58,060
But I can't let you have it for free.

90
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:01,000
Only family and friends will be attending.

91
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,260
It'll be about fifty people.
How much will it cost?

92
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:05,660
I can make the ceremony free for you.

93
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,400
As for the reception...

94
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:11,080
Well, even at a low estimate,
it's twenty thousand yen per person.

95
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:13,440
Twenty thousand yen times fifty...

96
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,640
That's a million yen?

97
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:18,700
You've got to be joking.

98
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:21,660
There's no way I can pay that kind of money.

99
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:26,320
Hey, you don't know the common sense of the world,
so you're being naive about it.

100
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:31,680
Shut up, you damn brat! Even at New Year's and year-end parties,
it's five thousand yen per person for you.

101
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:37,420
Yeah, and you eat and drink plenty!
And you, a mere brat, are out chasing money!

102
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:42,140
Idiot! Don't lump a wedding
in with a New Year's party!

103
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:47,140
Well, that's true enough. There's the
kimono and the commemorative photos, too.

104
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,080
Yes.

105
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:50,100
Wait a minute.

106
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:57,600
The 13th next month is a
Friday and a butsumetsu day.

107
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:02,160
Kankichi, we have no wedding
bookings on that day at all.

108
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:04,160
Half price is fine.

109
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:05,480
Really?

110
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:09,040
Whether it's a butsumetsu day or Friday the 13th,
it doesn't matter.

111
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,280
All that matters is that
you hold the wedding.

112
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,480
Alright, that day it is.

113
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,640
Just handle the rest of the
arrangements however you like.

114
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:20,220
Eeeeeh!

115
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,120
Eeeeeh!

116
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:39,880
Instead of earning money for the wedding,
we've gone completely broke?

117
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:47,920
Sensei, well done!

118
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:52,020
Just as expected,
the swordsman the boss hired as a bodyguard.

119
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:55,340
Sensei, here's the rest of
the bodyguard fee we agreed on.

120
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:56,660
Please accept this.

121
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:58,140
W-wow, this is it!

122
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,180
Thanks for your business.

123
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:10,000
Ryo-san, we're really going to win, right?

124
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,580
If we lose, you'll have to pay back
half of the sukketto money, Ryo.

125
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:16,440
But the opposing team has three
former pro baseball players.

126
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,700
Are you sure you'll be all right?

127
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:21,920
Even if they have major leaguers
like McGwire and Sosa on their team,

128
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,500
as long as I'm in as a sukketto,
we'll never lose.

129
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:26,440
Fireball!

130
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,360
Already a former pro

131
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:35,260
But to earn 500,000 yen,
we can't afford to lose.

132
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,600
Yaaah!

133
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:42,980
How about that?

134
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:43,580
What?

135
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:44,840
The ball...

136
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:49,800
He'll never catch it chasing it like that.

137
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:52,720
Move, move, move, move, move, move, move!

138
00:08:53,780 --> 00:09:04,940
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

139
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,080
No, that's not it. Ryo-san is...

140
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:14,600
Two outs, two on, bases loaded,
I'll end it with one swing!

141
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,181
This is the only tough one,

142
00:09:17,231 --> 00:09:19,740
first base is open, so we'll walk him.

143
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:26,600
Oh my God!

144
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:39,360
Yes!

145
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:46,080
Whenever you want to win,
call our Tairyoku Corporation!

146
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,500
Hello, this is

147
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:55,660
Tairyoku Corporation? No, that's not us.

148
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:59,520
It's me! Give it here!
Hello, you're speaking with me now.

149
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,220
Yeah, yeah.

150
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,920
A baseball pitcher, right?

151
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,480
When's the game?

152
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,360
Hold on a moment, please.

153
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:11,600
I'm free from 9:30 to 11 in the morning.

154
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,040
Is that OK? Where's the place?

155
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,100
Yeah, yeah, got it.

156
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:19,280
The helper fee is paid in advance,
so bank transfer or

157
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:22,060
please have the cash ready before the match.

158
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:25,720
So, from 9:30 to 11:00, and

159
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:29,160
Alright, that's our target amount reached.

160
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,720
After the 13th, it'll be my pocket money.

161
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:34,640
Senpai,
you're starting another business again?

162
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:40,840
Yeah, well, there's a reason I have
to earn 500,000 yen by the 13th.

163
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,680
I started a company
called Tairyoku Co., Ltd.

164
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,860
Tairyoku Co., Ltd.

165
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:49,940
From softball and gateball to mahjong,
moving, and weeding.

166
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:54,220
It's a company that takes on helpers
for every kind of sport and job.

167
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:56,460
Still, what an incredible schedule.

168
00:10:56,460 --> 00:11:00,780
Seriously, even your lunch breaks are
filled with gateball matches every day.

169
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,340
Look at this!

170
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,760
You've been wearing that shirt for over ten days,
haven't you?

171
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:09,260
Wrong! It's the body underneath!

172
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,080
Behold this trained, supple body!

173
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,380
Superhuman stamina and explosive speed!

174
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:18,600
A man works his body hard to earn money.
That's the proper way!

175
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:21,400
Trying to make money the easy way,
what a sleazy guy!

176
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:24,080
That's strange!
You're usually the sleazy one.

177
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:24,840
Ugh!

178
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,640
Urgh!

179
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:27,640
Say whatever you like!

180
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:31,760
But you came up with a good one, senpai.
It's the perfect business for you!

181
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:36,760
Right? Only a week into the job
and I've already made 250,000 yen.

182
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,480
What's this about 250,000 yen?

183
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,680
N-no, Chief!

184
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:43,960
N-nothing!

185
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:47,560
Chief, aren't you going to
the squad leaders' meeting?

186
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:50,240
Then I'm leaving things to you.

187
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:54,640
And Ryo.

188
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:58,280
I'm counting on you at the
judo tournament on the 12th.

189
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:01,060
I completely forgot.

190
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:05,240
The station chief said he's looking
forward to coming to cheer you on.

191
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:07,700
Listen, win the Zekahi too.

192
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:08,740
Got it?

193
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:11,720
Hey, winning doesn't get us anything,
does it?

194
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,360
Did you say something?

195
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,460
Nothing.

196
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,580
Come on, off you go!

197
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:22,060
What time does the Nakagawa judo tournament run,
from when to when?

198
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,020
It starts at 12:00.

199
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:27,660
If we keep winning,
the final should be around five o'clock.

200
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:28,700
Well, this is a problem.

201
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:34,080
On the 12th, from 5 a.m. to 11 a.m.,
there are four sandlot baseball games.

202
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:37,540
After noon, there's a rugby match
and the neighborhood swim meet.

203
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:42,120
On top of that, I have to attend the ballet
recital and caddy four rounds of golf.

204
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,220
What did you say?

205
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,160
That's true.

206
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,640
Even for a senior officer,
that's impossible.

207
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,420
No, once we've taken a job on,
we always see it through

208
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,800
that's the motto of Tairyoku Co.

209
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,540
We'll make sure to get it done.

210
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,140
Ippon! That's the match!

211
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,860
The next round is about to start, and yet

212
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,480
what is Ryotsu doing?

213
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,800
He said he'd be here by noon.

214
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,460
Sorry I'm late.

215
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:31,940
Senpai.

216
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:34,880
Ryotsu, after all I told you,
you're really something.

217
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,080
Chief, there's no time to be angry.

218
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,180
Ryo-chan, hurry and change!

219
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,960
The last match went into overtime.

220
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:46,940
So you won all four
matches since early morning?

221
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,960
Of course.
If I lost, my fee would've been cut in half.

222
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:54,100
I didn't want to enter
a mere match like this.

223
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:57,000
Don't say that, just hurry up!

224
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:00,760
We will now begin the fifth
match of the first round.

225
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,420
Katsushika Prize, Ryotsu-kun.

226
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:04,040
Out Prize, Yamada-kun.

227
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:07,560
Let's finish this quickly.
A match like this won't make us any money.

228
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:08,400
Begin.

229
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:12,060
Green Chat.

230
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:13,660
Ippon.

231
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:16,880
Fast.

232
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,840
It was decided in one second.

233
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:26,940
Senpai, that was masterful.

234
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,280
You did it, Ryo-chan.

235
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,060
I'll be back in 30 minutes.

236
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:31,760
Yes.

237
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:43,940
Oh no, it's already started!

238
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:47,360
Ryo-san's late. He hasn't forgotten, has he?

239
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:51,160
No, he should be here.
It's a match with money on the line.

240
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:56,480
Is Ryo-san here? He's competing in
the men's youth division 50kg class.

241
00:14:56,480 --> 00:14:58,320
If he's not here, he'll be disqualified.

242
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:00,760
Yes, yes, yes! I'm coming right now!

243
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:02,760
Robo-san, don't scare me like that!

244
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,800
The schedule's slipped a bit.
Sorry about that.

245
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,200
Sorry.

246
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,480
Sorry.

247
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:17,100
Amazing.

248
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,000
W-wow!

249
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:28,800
I'm a fish that's been turned into a fillet!

250
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:41,100
Overwhelming strength that keeps everyone at bay!
This is incredible!

251
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:42,880
That's amazing, Ryo-san!

252
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:47,680
The next 100m freestyle is at 1:30, right?

253
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:50,840
I've got a lot on my plate right now.

254
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,860
I'll definitely be back by 1:30.

255
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:53,540
See ya.

256
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,060
Ryo-san.

257
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:58,580
Ryotsu still hasn't shown up?

258
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:00,740
He said he'd definitely come, though.

259
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,260
Hey.

260
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:03,940
Sorry to keep you waiting.

261
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:04,480
There you are.

262
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:05,580
Hurry up, come on.

263
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,040
Kickoff's almost here!

264
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:20,680
Ryotsu!

265
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:21,920
Leave it to me!

266
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:23,800
Don't push!

267
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:45,660
Yes! As expected of the
Human Machine Gun, Ryotsu!

268
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:49,320
Not just as a helper,
we really want you to join our rugby team!

269
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,800
Ow

270
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:53,740
Hey, what happened?

271
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,440
Are you hurt?

272
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,540
Don't worry, I'm fine.

273
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,980
Ow

274
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:01,360
You shouldn't push yourself.
You're a valuable helper.

275
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,100
Why don't you rest on the bench for a bit?

276
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,680
Due to the referee's injury,
we'll make a temporary player substitution.

277
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:10,520
That team is strong, but if we just
show our faces here and there, we'll win.

278
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:13,600
Oh no, the game's already starting!

279
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,140
Wow

280
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:22,300
Kelly-san, you're here!

281
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,480
You're safe.

282
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:27,680
Then, sir, carry this and do your best.

283
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:30,360
Aren't you the one who's going to carry it?

284
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,860
It's not like you get to
keep whatever's left over.

285
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:32,800
Yes.

286
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:37,540
Then, you two,
drive the carts yourselves and move along.

287
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:39,680
Well, see you at the next hole!

288
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,720
Hey, hold on -

289
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:42,580
Wait, what?

290
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:48,480
Ryotsu-kun from Katsushika Station!
Is Ryotsu-kun from Katsushika Station here?

291
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:53,240
What? He's juggling caddie jobs for rugby,
swimming, and golf?

292
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:57,520
On top of that, he's apparently also helping
out at a ballet performance starting at three.

293
00:17:58,420 --> 00:17:59,300
That idiot!

294
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,820
Since he doesn't seem to be here,
we'll consider it a forfeit.

295
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:02,560
I'm right here!

296
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:04,780
Ryo-chan!

297
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,860
W-what's with that outfit?

298
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:12,360
The roads were jammed,
so it was such a hassle.

299
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:20,060
Ippon! That's the match.

300
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:22,240
Strong.

301
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:24,100
But the look is way too creepy.

302
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,300
What is that?

303
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:41,200
Even if it's for money,
this outfit is seriously embarrassing!

304
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:44,440
Hey, Takemoto,
how long are you going to keep staring?

305
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:45,540
Well, well.

306
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,980
Sorry I'm late.

307
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:51,660
Again...

308
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:56,020
Whoa! H-hey! What's with that outfit?!

309
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:59,156
I'm getting all confused.

310
00:18:59,206 --> 00:19:00,720
Even I find it creepy.

311
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:19,860
Are you all right, Senpai? You look pale.

312
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:24,720
I'm starting to think the
schedule was a little too much.

313
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:29,320
Ryotsu, you've made it all the way to the final,
so you'd better win!

314
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:31,200
Leave it to me.

315
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:34,940
We will now begin the championship match.

316
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:43,240
Of all people, I have to face this guy.

317
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,140
Damn it!

318
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:45,260
Hajime!

319
00:19:45,260 --> 00:20:07,600
Uuuuuuuuuughhhhhhhhhh...

320
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:08,540
What happened, Senpai?!

321
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:11,720
Looks like I've thrown my back out.

322
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:16,440
You should stop helping out
with side jobs today and rest.

323
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,120
Don't be ridiculous!

324
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,100
If I cancel, all that money is gone!

325
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:25,000
To reach 500,000 yen, I absolutely
have to win the final swimming event!

326
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:27,960
Nakagawa,
bring me something I can use as a cane!

327
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:28,520
Y-yes!

328
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:33,320
Ryotsu, what about the award ceremony?

329
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:35,360
Please have the Chief compete in your place.

330
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,900
I knew it, you've reached your limit.

331
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,600
I know that already.

332
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:42,860
But a man keeps the promises he makes,

333
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:44,860
no matter what happens.

334
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:47,680
As long as my body can move, I'll compete.

335
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:52,660
You're less devoted to being
a pro than you are to money.

336
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,560
The 200-meter freestyle is
finally nearing its climax.

337
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:57,960
Which athlete will win the gold?

338
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:00,920
My back hurts,
and I can't get any strength into it.

339
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:04,600
Whoops, I've turned into a fish myself.

340
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,980
The second-place swimmer is closing in fast!

341
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:09,680
He's been passed.

342
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,660
No good, I'm losing consciousness.

343
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:14,340
Kontag!

344
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:19,480
Damn it, I have to earn the
wedding money no matter what!

345
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:22,460
Ryotsu! What an incredible comeback!

346
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,920
Who's the winner? Who's the winner?

347
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,742
Ryotsu, 50...

348
00:21:28,792 --> 00:21:31,660
After the 100m, he wins the 200m too!

349
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:34,160
Yay, he's unbeatable!

350
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:35,540
How about that!

351
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,540
Hey! Ryo-san!

352
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,600
Ryo-san!

353
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:42,060
He's sinking! We have to save him quickly!

354
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:46,800
I kept my promise somehow, Kontag!

355
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:51,920
Don't even come to help out!

356
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,840
Where did Ryo-san go?!

357
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:58,000
We paid his helper fee for this morning's match in advance,
and now this!

358
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:02,180
W-wait, please!
Senpai has gone to the hospital right now!

359
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:06,260
Yesterday's hard schedule
made his lumbago even worse,

360
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,800
Well, even if you say that to me,

361
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:09,800
You promised, we had a deal, right?

362
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:16,380
I stopped by because I wanted to
thank Kan-chan before the wedding,

363
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,420
Is Ryo-chan here?

364
00:22:25,660 --> 00:22:28,180
Kankichi, how's your back holding up?

365
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,660
Since they gave me a painkiller shot,
it's better than yesterday.

366
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:34,940
Still, that Oshō place is ripping us off,
isn't it?

367
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,560
And there wasn't even a sea bream head.

368
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:39,160
At ten thousand yen a head,
it's a pretty decent spread.

369
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,180
Mom.

370
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:43,140
How can I ever thank Mom enough?

371
00:22:43,140 --> 00:22:45,680
You worked yourself so hard
you threw your back out.

372
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,440
Ugh, heave-ho!

373
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,640
The most beautiful bride in the land is ruined,
isn't she?

374
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,440
Be happy, you hear?

375
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,660
Yeah, thank you.

376
00:22:57,260 --> 00:22:58,820
Hey, is Ryo-san here?

377
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:02,260
Damn, they came all the
way here just to complain.

378
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:07,360
Ryo-san, we didn't come here to attack you.

379
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:10,520
Don't be so distant, Ryo-san.

380
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:14,380
If you were working so hard for this day,
you could have just said so.

381
00:23:14,380 --> 00:23:15,378
Ryo-san,

382
00:23:15,428 --> 00:23:18,400
sorry, but we're going to
liven things up on our own.

383
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,880
Hey, come on in!

384
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:22,630
Ussh, ussh,

385
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:26,600
Ussh, ussh, ussh!

386
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:29,660
It's the neighborhood association's mikoshi!

387
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,480
Even the shopping street's samba team!

388
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:40,400
Ryo-chan, I've changed my opinion of you!

389
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,560
Senpai, let's dance together!

390
00:23:43,020 --> 00:23:44,920
This makes me so happy!

391
00:23:45,620 --> 00:23:48,220
Konta, Shiori-san, come on,
let's dance together!

392
00:23:50,860 --> 00:23:52,300
Alright, let's go!

393
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:57,940
My lumbago is acting up again...

394
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:24,780
As I change, how will I look

395
00:24:25,340 --> 00:24:29,240
in your eyes?

396
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:33,580
After our fights, we always

397
00:24:33,580 --> 00:24:36,120
share a brief kiss.

398
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:40,240
Your teary eyes were so lovable.

399
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:45,420
Such irreplaceable things,

400
00:24:45,940 --> 00:24:49,060
how many will a person

401
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:50,880
get in a lifetime?

402
00:24:52,680 --> 00:25:02,280
You were me, and I was you,
and that alone was enough.

403
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:15,000
Just from you smiling,
every pain seemed to heal.

404
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:22,720
Well, next week

405
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:32,740
Enough already!

406
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:36,200
Next time: The Smiling Family, Ebisu-kun

407
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,120
See you then.

